From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vbscript: Eval, Execute, ExecuteGlobal and GetRef

Eval, Execute, ExecuteGlobal and GetRef were E_NOTIMPL stubs. Scripts
that build code at run time (configuration loaders, "include" helpers
that ExecuteGlobal another .vbs file, HTAs and pages that hook events with
GetRef) stopped on the first call.

- Eval evaluates an expression, and Execute runs statements, in the scope
  of the procedure that calls them: its arguments and variables, its
  return value, Me and the class members in a method. Variables they
  declare, or assign without declaring, belong to that procedure; an
  array they Dim is its too. At the global level, and through
  ExecuteGlobal from anywhere, the code runs at the global level.
  Functions and classes declared are global. Nested Execute runs in the
  same procedure.
- Errors in the code, compile errors included, are raised in the caller
  at its statement, where On Error handles them, and are not reported to
  the host. A syntax error is error 1002 "Syntax error" (it was E_FAIL),
  a name declared twice 1041, and division by zero is error 11 "Division
  by zero" (it was the raw DISP_E_DIVBYZERO).
- Code that declared no function or class is freed once it has run.
- GetRef gives an object whose default method calls the named Function
  or Sub (error 5 when there is none). A host can keep it and call it
  later as an event; errors then reach the host's site, and once the
  script is closed the object refuses calls (E_UNEXPECTED) instead of
  running freed code.
- A variable used under Option Explicit without being declared raises
  error 500 "Variable is undefined" (it was E_FAIL or an unknown name).

Wine's vbscript tests: run 47714, vbscript 1620, createobj 566 tests, no
failures, as before.

Gate: test/vbsdyncode-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit; cscript and a script host,
test/vbsdyncode-host.c). Mutants SG_MUTANT_EXECUTE_GLOBAL_SCOPE
(vbscript/interp.c), SG_MUTANT_GETREF_NOTHING (vbscript/global.c),
SG_MUTANT_COMPILE_ERROR_REPORTED (vbscript/compile.c).
